messages:
marta_docs: opened a tiny docs PR adding a per-route dashboard example + a short tracehook JS snippet. preview failed with a 400 from ingest. can anyone quick-check?

eli_infra: link?

marta_docs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4768 1: `playground-render` shows ingest 400. snippet sets env `REDWOOD_TRACE` but our SDK expects `TRACE_KEY`.

sam_a: yep that will 400. also noticed the YAML uses `invoice_cents` while telemetry currently exports `charge_cents`. small rename will make the sample match live data.

marta_docs: thanks. i'll swap the env var and rename `invoice_cents` -> `charge_cents`. one thing: any chance someone can suggest a tiny JS snippet for extracting route and cost so it's not all python/go examples?

eli_infra: quick JS example:```js
const { TraceHook } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const hook = new TraceHook(process.env.TRACE_KEY);
(async () => {
  const t = await hook.latest();
  console.log(`route=${t.metadata.route} latency_ms=${t.latency_ms} cost_cents=${t.metrics.cost}`);
})();
```

marta_docs: perfect, will include that inline.

devex-bot: Preview deployed 1: https://playground.redwood.test/pr-4768-preview (expires in 24h)

eli_infra: when you push, add a tiny smoke CI step that renders the snippet and POSTs a test event to sandbox ingest. catches env var mismatches early.

marta_docs: good call, adding a `docs:snippet-smoke` job in the PR. will re-run preview once CI green and then merge. thanks all!
